{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3neUe1DS4RjWcuAcX7D","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed \"wholsale\" to \"wholesale\" in the October, November and December files and committed it as one commit, `a15eba4`. Reverting that one commit undoes the fix.\n\n- **What changed:** one row in each of `data/2025-10.csv`, `data/2025-11.csv` and `data/2025-12.csv`. The check passed, and it does cover these 2025 files.\n- **Other occurrences:** a search of the whole repo found no other \"wholsale\" except `inbox/2025-12.csv`, which still has it. That file is gitignored, so it isn't part of the repo or the commit. I left it alone so the commit stays easy to revert. Say so if you want it fixed too.\n- **Commit message:** `2025-12:` is the newest of the three months, since the prefix takes one month and the commit covers three.\n- **January:** `data/2026-01.csv` is still untracked, as you asked.\n- **Invoices export:** I'm still waiting on your answer about plain copy versus filtering out segment C customers.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":333,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":721,"cache_read_input_tokens":18689,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":721,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-43>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:44:10.827Z","request_id":"gen-1794703447-q2baGhdeaPGvUiLBdDpG"}
